formatted_question:
In the paper 'FlashAttention-3: Fast and Accurate Attention with Asynchrony and Low-precision', \textsc{FlashAttention-3} can account for block quantization at no computation cost because
(A) it uses a single scale factor for each of \mathbf{Q}, \mathbf{K}, and \mathbf{V}
(B) its asynchronous pipeline hides the extra dequantization work
(C) quantizing \mathbf{Q}, \mathbf{K}, and \mathbf{V} separately removes any need to rescale \mathbf{S}
(D) it already operates on blocks
(E) the tensor cores natively fuse per-block quantization into the attention matmul
